{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they bear them iniquity of guilt.</b> Those who profane the sacred by feeding it to strangers — they bear them iniquity of guilt, namely to the strangers who eat it." "<b>The sacred gifts of theirs.</b> To teach you that their terumah is given to whichever priest they wish." "<b>From their sacred gifts.</b> It refers to the sacred gifts of the children of Israel."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:19.800959982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}